{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RED/GREEN evidence before commit:\n\n- Final RED with no implementation: 8 failures. The root conftest tests failed because time/pytest_fixture_setup/_timed_ci_call did not exist; the editor wiring test failed because _instrument_editor_server_setup did not exist. A first oracle attempt imported tests/unit/conftest.py by accident; per the strict test-modification guard, I removed the implementation, corrected the test to obtain the already-loaded root plugin, and re-proved this final RED before reapplying the implementation.\n- GREEN: 9 focused observer/wiring/loopback tests passed, then both full focused modules passed (24 tests in 4.61s). The same 24 tests passed under xdist -n 2 with CI=true in 3.48s; all 24 nodes collect and execute without skip/xfail.\n- Mutation proof: changing the threshold from 1.0s to 999.0s returned test_fixture_setup_hook_reports_worker_node_fixture_and_elapsed to RED with DID NOT WARN; restoring 1.0s returned the suite to GREEN.\n- Gates: worktree-venv make lint passed (2023 files formatted, actionlint/zizmor/complexity/DCO checks clean); worktree-venv make typecheck passed across 541 source files.\n- Safety: timing is disabled outside CI/REBAR_FIXTURE_TIMING=1, uses only monotonic clock + pytest warnings, adds no dependency/external call, and restores the constructor/bind/getfqdn callables before each editor test body. Original return objects and exception identity are covered."},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786746123321136001,"uuid":"960e99d5-8dda-4df2-869e-f0d6167376ee"}